What this repository and its release archives contain
  Only this project's own code and its own pre-compiled bridge assembly
  (bridge/DigitvaIcd11Bridge.dll, built from bridge/Bridge.cs, embedded in the
  binary). They contain no WHO assemblies and no WHO data. WHO has not given
  this project written permission to redistribute either.

What is downloaded, and from where
  When you run `who-icd11-server --bootstrap`, your machine downloads, directly
  from WHO's own sources and verified against SHA-256 digests pinned in
  src/bootstrap.rs:
    - the ICD-API 2.6.0 and DORIS 1.2.0 .NET assemblies, from the Docker Hub
      image whoicd/icd-api:2.6.0;
    - the ICD-11 2026-01 (English) release and search-index files, from
      icdcdn.who.int;
    - the DORIS 1.2.0 rule files, from icd11files.blob.core.windows.net.
  Those files are not part of this project. Use of them is governed by WHO's
  terms, not by this project's MIT licence.

WHO content and trademarks
  ICD-11 content is licensed by WHO under Creative Commons
  Attribution-NoDerivatives 3.0 IGO (CC BY-ND 3.0 IGO) and keeps WHO's
  attribution. ICD-API, DORIS and CoDEdit are WHO's. tests/fixtures (git repository only)
  contains example death certificates used as test inputs; any ICD-11 codes and titles in
